  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The short answer",
      "items": [
        "A session is one SAM instance",
        "Its prompt is assembled from the role persona, operator memory, and the compact skill index",
        "then the loop alternates between calling Claude and dispatching the tools it asks for"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown here",
      "items": [
        "The guard pipeline around each tool call, and everything after the session closes",
        "Connected but out of scope: Email gateway, Cron scheduler, Memory manager, Skill store, Tool registry, Security gate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Doctrine",
      "items": [
        "A session's role picks its model, token budget, iteration cap, persona, and visible tool set together, in lockstep. — Mixing an action model with a read-only tool schema produces a session that is neither, so an unknown role normalises to the full action profile rather than a half-configured one."
      ]
    }
  ]
